                                "text": "\"Smash the nuclear family\" was a common slogan in the Women's Movement of the early 1970's. It went along with a general hostility to families, motherhood, being a housewife — any role that seemed at all traditionally female. To want to be a mother somehow seemed an unliberated desire."
